# Copper Linux -- the components startniri installs before it starts niri.
#
# Three whitespace-separated columns:
#
#   <name>   <probe>                       <how>
#
# <probe> is a path that exists when the component is present. startniri
# installs the missing ones whose <how> is "ingot", by asking ingot
# for them.
# <how> of "image" means this stage already ships it in the ISO: it is
# kept in this list so the report is honest about what a desktop is
# supposed to have, but ingot has no such package and the launcher will
# not try to install one -- a missing "image" component is a broken
# image, said out loud.
#
# The ingot payloads below are the ones a fresh session is expected to have:
# the terminal tools (btop, fastfetch, vim), the browser, and the two things
# every command line reaches for (curl, git). Each payload carries its own
# dependency closure, so the first start downloads a few hundred MB; only the
# ones actually missing are installed, and ingot reports each failure without
# stopping the rest. --no declines the whole set once for a machine that stays
# offline, and later starts install nothing because the probes are present.

btop                 /usr/bin/btop                ingot
fastfetch            /usr/bin/fastfetch           ingot
firefox              /usr/bin/firefox             ingot
curl                 /usr/bin/curl                ingot
git                  /usr/bin/git                 ingot
vim                  /usr/bin/vim                 ingot

# The gui stage already ships make and nano, and ping is busybox's applet.
# Their probes pass, so they are never installed; they are listed so the
# manifest is the whole answer to "what does this session have".
make                 /usr/bin/make                image
nano                 /usr/bin/nano                image
ping                 /bin/ping                    image

niri                 /usr/bin/niri                image
kitty                /usr/bin/kitty               image
waybar               /usr/bin/waybar               image
swaybg               /usr/bin/swaybg               image
swaync               /usr/bin/swaync               image
fuzzel               /usr/bin/fuzzel               image
polkit-agent         /usr/lib/policykit-1-gnome/polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1 image
